WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.000
Hello, let's create a Compute Engine disk image.

00:00:03.166 --> 00:00:08.900
To start out with, I have a virtual machine that I have configured, and want to use as a template for my new image.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.875
The first step is to delete my virtual machine, but I want to save the boot persistent disk.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
So, I use gcloud compute instances delete, then the name of the VM, and the option to keep disks, boot.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:34.625
Now, I create an image from that disk with gcloud compute images create, then the name that I want to give the new image, and then specify the source persistent disk.

00:00:35.583 --> 00:00:46.916
Now that we have the image, I can create new VMs from that image with gcloud compute instances create, then specify the new image name and the name of the VM.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:55.833
Now, we can SSH into the VM, and here you can see that our new VM has the same configuration as the original template VM.

